Enable themes and the keyboard-shortcut tray in the desktop app

Purpose:
Bring two web-app features to the desktop wrapper: selectable themes
and the keyboard-shortcut tray.

Approach:
- View > Theme native menu (Default/Classic/Gray/Green/Turquoise/Dark),
  forwarded to Elm as a ThemeChanged Incoming message and applied via
  the existing Page.Doc.Theme; persisted per file and restored on open.
- Doc.UI.viewShortcuts tray, its open state persisted per file via
  SaveUserSetting ("shortcutTrayOpen"), closed by default so new
  documents don't open with the tray showing.
- Desktop layout (desktop.css): the desktop has no header bar, so the
  collapsed tray icon is pinned to the top edge (the web app's 40px
  offset left it floating); the save indicator sits left of the toggle
  icon and disappears behind the open tray panel (z-index). Toggling the
  tray closes any open tooltip, as in the web app.

Constraints:
- Reuse the web app's theme and tray code; only the desktop wrapper and
  desktop.css change their placement and persistence.

